@startuml
title SplitSmart payment request and committed payment lifecycle

[*] --> Received : validly shaped request
Received --> Failed : authorization / validation / policy failure
Received --> Posted : pair valid; transaction commits
Posted --> Reversed : approved compensating action [policy open]
Failed --> [*]
Posted --> [*]
Reversed --> [*]

note right of Posted
PostedPayment is a committed financial fact and has exactly one LedgerEntry.
The payment and posting commit atomically. A duplicate request resolves to the
same posted result and does not create another payment or posting.
end note
note right of Failed
Failed request is not a Payment financial fact and has no ledger entry.
Retry/idempotency retention and semantic duplicate rules require approval.
end note
note bottom
Pending external transfer/settlement is not currently defined. If introduced,
model it as a non-posted PaymentAttempt with no LedgerEntry until committed.
Reversal semantics remain open.
end note
@enduml
